WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.487
Welcome to the WhatsApp Customer Care course. Module one.

2
00:00:04.487 --> 00:00:08.949
The basics of the WhatsApp Business API, and a tour of the dashboard.

3
00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:16.091
Customers already live on WhatsApp. For Oribrix, that makes it one of the best

4
00:00:16.091 --> 00:00:20.541
Places to answer questions, send order updates and win back customers.

5
00:00:20.541 --> 00:00:25.753
This course shows you how the WhatsApp Business API platform works, so you can use

6
00:00:25.753 --> 00:00:26.706
It confidently.

7
00:00:27.156 --> 00:00:30.143
First, what the WhatsApp Business API actually is.

8
00:00:30.593 --> 00:00:33.878
Then how it differs from the normal WhatsApp app on your phone.

9
00:00:34.328 --> 00:00:36.654
Then the four main ways businesses use it.

10
00:00:37.104 --> 00:00:40.048
Then what a business needs before it can be onboarded.

11
00:00:40.498 --> 00:00:43.207
Then the daily message limits that Meta sets.

12
00:00:43.657 --> 00:00:46.046
And finally, a tour of the main dashboard.

13
00:00:48.433 --> 00:00:53.764
The WhatsApp Business API is designed for medium and large businesses that need to

14
00:00:53.764 --> 00:00:57.990
Talk to customers at scale. Let's compare it with the normal app.

15
00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:02.618
The normal WhatsApp app is one phone and one person typing by hand.

16
00:01:02.618 --> 00:01:07.294
It has no connection to your systems, and it's fine for a handful of chats.

17
00:01:07.744 --> 00:01:13.221
The Business API lets several agents share one number, sends messages automatically

18
00:01:13.221 --> 00:01:18.699
From your system, connects to your website, app or C R M, and handles large volumes

19
00:01:18.699 --> 00:01:23.780
Of chats. Brands use it for alerts, O T Ps, order updates and offers, because

20
00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:28.928
WhatsApp messages have some of the highest open and read rates of any channel.

21
00:01:31.333 --> 00:01:34.764
There are four main ways to use the WhatsApp Business API.

22
00:01:34.764 --> 00:01:39.674
For customer care, the second and fourth matter most, but you should know all four.

23
00:01:40.124 --> 00:01:45.377
One, marketing. Sending promotional messages to customers who have opted in, without

24
00:01:45.377 --> 00:01:50.442
Risking the number getting banned. You can manage opt-ins and opt-outs, and track

25
00:01:50.442 --> 00:01:51.943
Delivery and read rates.

26
00:01:52.393 --> 00:01:58.084
Two, live chat and a shared inbox. Up to fifteen agents can log in from mobile or

27
00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:01.246
Desktop and chat with customers in real time.

28
00:02:01.696 --> 00:02:07.948
Three, API integration. Your website or app sends messages automatically, like O T

29
00:02:07.948 --> 00:02:13.667
Ps, alerts and order updates. It can also connect to shops like Shopify and

30
00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:14.582
WooCommerce.

31
00:02:15.032 --> 00:02:20.408
Four, the chatbot. An automatic assistant that answers common questions, captures

32
00:02:20.408 --> 00:02:25.784
Leads and guides customers, built with a drag and drop builder, no coding needed.

33
00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:31.617
Before a business can use the API, it needs four things.

34
00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:34.301
Onboarding itself is free with the platform.

35
00:02:34.751 --> 00:02:39.592
A phone number that is not on WhatsApp at all. Not on the normal app and not on

36
00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:42.901
WhatsApp Business. If it is, it must be removed first.

37
00:02:43.351 --> 00:02:45.228
A Facebook page, or a website.

38
00:02:45.678 --> 00:02:48.366
A Facebook account that is at least six months old.

39
00:02:48.816 --> 00:02:55.067
And business documents for verification, such as G S T or M S M E registration.

40
00:02:57.467 --> 00:03:01.110
Remember this, because it's the most common onboarding mistake.

41
00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:05.737
The number you connect to the API must not already be on WhatsApp, in either the

42
00:03:05.737 --> 00:03:10.537
Normal app or the WhatsApp Business app. Use a fresh number, or delete the WhatsApp

43
00:03:10.537 --> 00:03:15.279
Account from it first. Once it is on the API, you won't be able to use that number

44
00:03:15.279 --> 00:03:16.262
In the phone app.

45
00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:12.486
Meta sets a daily limit on how many people you can message.

46
00:04:12.486 --> 00:04:15.797
It starts small and grows as you show good behaviour.

47
00:04:16.247 --> 00:04:19.575
At the start, the limit is around two thousand people per day.

48
00:04:20.025 --> 00:04:23.524
Once the business account is verified, you can begin to grow.

49
00:04:23.974 --> 00:04:29.078
Meta watches how your campaigns perform. Messages people want, and few blocks or

50
00:04:29.078 --> 00:04:30.993
Reports, count in your favour.

51
00:04:31.443 --> 00:04:33.811
The limit can rise to ten thousand per day.

52
00:04:34.261 --> 00:04:39.277
And over time up to one lakh per day. Spammy messages do the opposite and can get

53
00:04:39.277 --> 00:04:40.639
The number restricted.

54
00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:46.207
After logging in, the first screen is the main dashboard.

55
00:04:46.207 --> 00:04:47.321
Here's what's on it.

56
00:04:47.771 --> 00:04:52.805
Live status. Once the Facebook account and number are connected, the account shows

57
00:04:52.805 --> 00:04:53.296
As live.

58
00:04:53.746 --> 00:04:57.160
The daily messaging limit set by Meta, which we just covered.

59
00:04:57.610 --> 00:05:02.384
Profile and display picture. The picture and About text that customers see.

60
00:05:02.384 --> 00:05:05.631
Keep the Oribrix logo and a clear description here.

61
00:05:06.081 --> 00:05:10.753
Wallet credit. Messages are paid from this balance, so check it before a big

62
00:05:10.753 --> 00:05:12.844
Campaign and recharge when needed.

63
00:05:13.294 --> 00:05:19.047
WhatsApp link and Q R. Create a link or Q R code that opens a chat with Oribrix.

64
00:05:19.047 --> 00:05:22.787
It's useful on invoices, visiting cards and posters.

65
00:05:23.237 --> 00:05:27.013
And the website widget, a small WhatsApp chat button for the website.

66
00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.427
A few words you'll hear throughout this course.

67
00:05:31.877 --> 00:05:35.653
W A B A, the WhatsApp Business Account that lives with Meta.

68
00:05:36.103 --> 00:05:41.495
B S P, Business Solution Provider. The company whose platform you use to run the

69
00:05:41.495 --> 00:05:43.719
API, like the one in this course.

70
00:05:44.169 --> 00:05:47.636
Template. A message format that Meta approves in advance.

71
00:05:47.636 --> 00:05:49.886
You need one to start a conversation.

72
00:05:50.336 --> 00:05:55.496
Opt-in and opt-out. Whether the customer agreed to receive messages, or asked to

73
00:05:55.496 --> 00:05:55.819
Stop.

74
00:05:56.269 --> 00:06:01.459
And the twenty four hour window. After a customer messages you, you can reply freely

75
00:06:01.459 --> 00:06:05.229
For twenty four hours. After that, you need a template again.

76
00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:12.250
Quick check. Oribrix wants to connect its office number, which is already on the

77
00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:16.060
WhatsApp Business app. What must happen first? Think for a moment.

78
00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:23.751
The answer: WhatsApp must be removed from that number first.

79
00:06:23.751 --> 00:06:26.495
An API number cannot be on any WhatsApp app.

80
00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:31.028
Let's summarise module one.

81
00:06:31.478 --> 00:06:36.662
The API gives you many agents on one number, automation, integrations and scale.

82
00:06:37.112 --> 00:06:41.144
It's used for marketing, live chat, automatic alerts and chatbots.

83
00:06:41.594 --> 00:06:46.292
To start, you need a fresh number, a Facebook page or website, a six month old

84
00:06:46.292 --> 00:06:48.762
Facebook account, and business documents.

85
00:06:49.212 --> 00:06:52.881
The daily limit starts around two thousand and grows with good use.

86
00:06:53.331 --> 00:06:58.416
And the dashboard shows status, limit, profile, wallet, link and Q R, and the

87
00:06:58.416 --> 00:07:02.313
Website widget. In module two, we create message templates.

88
00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:09.159
That's the end of module 1. Next up, module 2: Message templates.
